ookbook:Ounce|oz]] (55 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[cookbook:butter|butter]]\n* ½ ea. [[cookbook:onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* ½ ea. [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]], chopped\n* ½ stalk [[cookbook:celery|celery]], chopped\n* [[cookbook:bacon|Bacon]], chopped\n* White [[cookbook:stock|stock]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[cookbook:tomato|tomato]] purée\n* [[cookbook:sage|Sage]]\n* [[cookbook:parsley|Parsley]]\n* [[cookbook:Parmesan Cheese|Parmesan cheese]], [[Cookbook:Grating|grated]]\n* [[cookbook:salt|Salt]]\n* [[cookbook:pepper|Pepper]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# [[Cookbook:Blanching|Blanch]] the cauliflower, then break into small bunches.\n# Melt the butter in a pot, then add the chopped onion, carrot, celery, and bacon. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] until softened.\n# Add white stock and [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] for a few minutes. [[Cookbook:Straining|Strain]] the stock to remove the solids.\n# Mix the tomato purée into the stock, then bring to a boil.\n# Mix in the cauliflower, sage, and parsley. Bring to a boil.\n# Mix in grated parmesan and pepper.\n# Serve with additional grated parmesan.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bacon]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Italian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cauliflower]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parmesan]]\n[[Category:Recipes using broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Soup alla Canavese","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ ea. cauliflower","sourceText":"½ ea. cauliflower","amountText":"½ ea. cauliflower","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 oz (55 g) butter","sourceText":"2 oz (55 g) butter","amountText":"2 oz (55 g) butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ ea. onion, chopped","sourceText":"½ ea. 